  model: "ASA class describes how sick the patient is, not how stressful the procedure is or which drugs you will use. A well-controlled hypertensive can tolerate a short restoration better than a long surgical removal of a third molar, because pain and fear release more catecholamine during the longer procedure. I would add functional capacity, today's vital signs against the baseline, the invasiveness of the procedure and the drug plan. The result may be routine care, a stress-reduced visit, a medical consultation or deferral."
